&lt;li&gt;Degree in Human Resources, Business Management, or related fields is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Poland employment legislation and its practical application in a business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interpersonal and influencing skills. Ability to communicate effectively at&amp;nbsp;all levels of the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of integrity and discretion in handling sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing monthly Payroll inputs to ensure that employees receive a&amp;nbsp;positive pay day experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an international or multi-site environment, to assist new jurisdiction&amp;nbsp;within your Ebury career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with HR technology and systems (e.g., HiBOB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organised with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English and Polish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
